  "description": "SAQVUD crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H62 Dy4 N24 O8 2+,C60 H62 Dy4 N24 O8 2+,4(Cl1 1-),42(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy5 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.768-3.785 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.38-114.18°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(L1-2H)2(L1-H)2(OH)4]Cl2·8H2O (crystal data: C60H62Dy4N24O8·2Cl·21H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
